{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and the endpoint accepted it.\n\n**Root cause:** The `recommendation` Service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`, so ClusterIP traffic only reached recommendation pods on the caller's node. The frontend runs on `kind-worker2`, while recommendation was on `kind-worker`, so every call from the frontend timed out (`ETIMEDOUT 10.96.17.192:8080`) and `/api/recommendations` returned 500.\n\n**Changes applied:**\n- Set `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster` on the `recommendation` Service, the default the other services use.\n- Removed the `kind-worker` nodeSelector from the `recommendation` deployment so it schedules normally.\n- Restarted the `frontend` deployment to clear the stale gRPC channel.\n\n**Verification:** `/api/recommendations` returns 200 in about 13 ms, `/api/products` still returns 200, and the frontend logs no new `ETIMEDOUT` errors.\n\nThe `frontend` deployment still has a nodeSelector pinning it to `kind-worker2`. I left it because it isn't causing the failure. It is worth reviewing, since it is unusual for a Helm-managed deployment."}}
